            <ArticleTitle>Botulinum toxin type A (Botox) in the treatment of migraine and other headaches.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>27-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Botulinum toxin type A (Botox) is increasingly used in the management of migraine and tension-type headaches. The results from small placebo-controlled trials and extensive open-label experience has suggested a significant role for this neurotoxin in the management of refractory headache. Several large placebo-controlled trials of episodic and chronic migraine are currently underway.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
